              "stepName": "State the result and its scope",
              "explanation": "Redo restores the committed update if it was not already reflected on disk.\n\n**Detailed reasoning and validation.** A committed transaction can be durable even when its changed page is still only in memory, provided the engine's log protocol has durably recorded the necessary information. After a crash, redo inspects log and page progress to apply updates not already reflected in persistent data pages. Reapplying must be safe across repeated interrupted recovery attempts, often using log-sequence comparisons or an equivalent mechanism. This example is intentionally abstract and does not specify an engine's exact redo algorithm. A restored logical value should match the committed transaction, whereas an uncommitted concurrent update must not be reported as a committed outcome."
