              "explanation": "Prepared participants may block until a durable decision is recovered.\n\n**Detailed reasoning and validation.** During the prepare phase of two-phase commit, participants may have logged a prepared state and retained locks while awaiting a final decision. If the coordinator fails before its durable commit/abort decision becomes available, those participants cannot simply decide on their own without risking disagreement. They may remain blocked until the coordinator or recovery mechanism resolves the outcome. The approach addresses atomic agreement under stated assumptions but can harm availability during failures. A saga uses local commits and compensating steps instead; compensation does not retroactively erase external effects such as a notification or payment processing fee."
